course: dictionary
lesson: 7395
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To know which meaning is meant, look at the context: the sentence and the words around the word. «Po» is a good example because it has several meanings.
explain: Read this: «Sam and Jake have an inside joke: whenever anyone says «potato», they both shout «PO-TAH-TO» like a posh butler.» Here PO is part of a silly word in a joke. It is not a box, a river or a bowl.
explain: Now read: «In Kung Fu Panda, Po gobbles dumplings.» Po is a name, because it is a character in a film. Capital letters, the film title and what Po does all give you the clue. Ask: what would fit here? A name fits, but a river does not.
explain: The same letters can mean something very different in another sentence, like a PO Box at the post office. Always check the words around the word before you choose its meaning.
fact: A word with several meanings is called a word with many meanings. The context shows which one is meant.
fact: «Po» can mean a chamber pot, PO (Post Office), a river in Italy, or a name.
fact: A chamber pot is an old-fashioned bowl kept under the bed for wee at night, before indoor toilets.
fact: PO stands for Post Office, as in «PO Box», a box at the post office where letters can be collected.
fact: The Po is the longest river in Italy, and it flows to the Adriatic Sea.
exercise: Sam and Jake shout «PO-TAH-TO» like a posh butler as a joke. What kind of joke is it? | A joke about a chamber pot | A joke about a river in Italy | *A joke about saying potato in a posh way | A joke about the post office
exercise: «In Kung Fu Panda, Po gobbles dumplings.» What kind of word is Po here? | *A name | A bowl under the bed | A box for letters | A river
exercise: Tom posts his letter to a «PO Box» at the post office. What does PO mean here? | *Post Office | Petty officer | Potato | Purchase order
test: In history lessons about Victorian homes, people used a po at night. What is a po? | *A bowl kept under the bed for wee at night | A box at the post office | A river in Italy | A name for a character
test: «The Po flows across northern Italy to the Adriatic Sea.» What is the Po here? | A chamber pot | A character in a film | A petty officer in the navy | *A river
exam: You read «Po gobbles dumplings» and «PO Box» and need to know which meaning of po each one uses. What should you do? | *Read the words around po and check which meaning makes sense | Pick the first meaning you remember and move on | Look only at the letters, not the sentence | Skip the sentence because po is too hard
